ub_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/comments/5163307961","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/issues/70968#issuecomment-5163307961","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/70968","id":5163307961,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAgUK288AAAABM8HTuQ","user":{"login":"takayoshi-makabe","id":48040599,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MDQwNTk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48040599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe","html_url":"https://github.com/takayoshi-makabe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-03T07:04:04Z","updated_at":"2026-08-03T07:04:04Z","body":"`dag_processor_log_target` was originally added in 2.4.0 (#25754) as a genuine exclusive switch: the `airflow.processor` logger's Python logging handler was swapped between a file handler and a stdout handler, so setting it to `stdout` meant no file was ever created.\n\nWhen the Dag File Processor was rewritten onto the Task SDK's subprocess/structlog architecture (around 3.0/3.1), that handler-swap mechanism was dropped entirely, and the config option silently stopped doing anything.\n\n#65528 (merged 2026-04-20) reconnected the option, but wired it into the `subprocess_logs_to_stdout` flag that already existed for **task** logs. That flag is intentionally additive for task logs — it duplicates output to stdout while always keeping the file, which makes sense there because task logs are served via the Log API and can be uploaded to remote storage, so the file is load-bearing.\n\nDag processor logs have neither of those dependencies (no API/UI route serves them, and they're never uploaded to remote storage), so there's no structural reason to force a file write when `dag_processor_log_target = stdout`. The current behavior (always write the file, optionally also duplicate to stdout) matches what #65528 intended for containers, but doesn't restore the original exclusive semantics that the config's own docs still describe (\"Where to send dag parser logs. If 'file', logs are sent to log files...\").\n\n---\nDrafted-by: Claude Code (Sonnet 5); reviewed by @takayoshi-makabe before posting","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/comments/5163307961/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"takayoshi-makabe","id":48040599,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MDQwNTk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48040599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe","html_url":"https://github.com/takayoshi-makabe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takayoshi-makabe/orgs","repos_ur